cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use this benchmark software, please cite the specific software
  release using the metadata below. If you use or discuss the study's
  empirical findings, also cite the associated Zenodo research paper
  provided under preferred-citation.

type: software

title: "KV-Cache vs. SPA: Research Benchmark and Reproducibility Package"

abstract: >-
  This repository provides the experimental implementation and
  reproducibility resources for a controlled longitudinal evaluation
  of Symbolic Persona Anchoring (SPA) and direct Transformer Key-Value
  (KV) cache interventions. The benchmark comprises a balanced
  6 × 10 × 4 factorial design, covering six experimental arms (A1–A6),
  ten open-weight language models (3B–14B), and four persona archetypes,
  yielding 240 trajectories and 12,000 conversational turns across
  50-turn rollouts.

  The implementation covers prompt-channel baselines and symbolic
  anchoring (A1 Raw History, A2 Generic Reminder, A3 Continuous SPA),
  alongside three implemented multi-turn adaptations of direct KV-cache
  interventions (A4 Belitsky-style additive steering, A5 Sun-style
  mid-layer trajectory transplantation, and A6 Memory Inception
  latent pre-RoPE KV banks).

  The research package includes model and experimental-arm registries,
  deterministic SHA-256 scenario seeding, persona and stressor
  generation, dedicated KV-cache intervention modules, semantic
  preservation and lexical-diversity metrics, statistical analysis,
  trajectory exports, and independent verification resources.

  The four-stage verification protocol covers archive and corpus
  integrity, implementation dispatch and AST auditing, bitwise
  recomputation of metrics across all 12,000 turns, and inferential
  statistical reproduction. A4–A6 are explicitly treated as
  implemented multi-turn methodological adaptations rather than
  exact reproductions of the original published pipelines.

